Confirmed and decisive: **`bt.momentum_signals` is a constant long (+1) position for 9/10 assets at every lookback** (0 sign flips), because it thresholds `mean(log(price))` — the mean of log *prices*, which is always > 0 for any asset priced above $1 — instead of the trailing *return*. Only NVDA flips once (its adjusted price starts at $0.16 < $1). The conventional trailing-return momentum flips 500–1200 times. This explains the identical medians across lookbacks 3/5/10 and means the "momentum edge" is unconditional equity beta, not momentum.

This is directly decision-relevant to the cost result. Let me add a self-contained signal-degeneracy diagnostic to the check artifact so the finding is reproducible and independently verifiable.
